cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Noophorics: a quantitative science of transferring understanding across heterogeneous minds"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-28
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/vyakymenko/noophorics"
abstract: >-
  Noophorics is a research program that measures the transfer of understanding
  between systems with non-identical priors — human to model, model to model,
  and a session to its own compacted successor. It replaces symbol recovery
  with behavioral convergence as the criterion of successful transfer, which
  yields measurable quantities: transfer fidelity relative to a stated probe
  measure, noophoric efficiency, channel capacity between minds, and phantom
  agreement — the gap between the parties' confidence that understanding
  occurred and the evidence that it did. The repository contains the axiomatic
  foundation, six falsifiable conjectural laws, ten open problems, a
  dependency-free reference implementation of the metrics, and pre-registered
  experiments.
keywords:
  - noophorics
  - transfer fidelity
  - phantom agreement
  - probe measure
  - agent handoff
  - context compaction
  - multi-agent systems
  - indeterminacy of translation
authors:
  - name: "The Noophorics Project"
    website: "https://github.com/vyakymenko/noophorics"
